# Upgrade ProjectFlow Edu Frontend to SaaS-Quality Platform

This plan outlines the frontend upgrades required to turn ProjectFlow Edu into a live-ready college project management system. It introduces a comprehensive team system (max 5 students), a robust marks and timeliness scoring system, final submission handling with GitHub validation, and real-time dashboard enhancements across all roles. The UI will be upgraded to have a clean, SaaS-quality feel while adhering strictly to existing design languages and standard Javascript/React practices (no TS, no Firebase).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The requirements specify calculating dummy real-time scores based on contribution, tasks, timeliness, and mentor feedback. Because we are relying on a dummy state for now, these scores will be mocked algorithmically or stored in local dummy context, prepared for future `Socket.io` and `MySQL/Axios` integration. Is this approach acceptable for the demo?

> [!WARNING]
> Since we are mocking new backend APIs (`/api/projects`, `/api/tasks`, `/api/submissions`, `/api/evaluations`), I will extend the `src/lib/api.js` (or mock data service) with dummy responses that match the expected MySQL schemas. 

